details:
(a) the year-wise and State-wise utilisation of the Nirbhaya Fund during the last five years against the total corpus allocated;
(b) the specific safety infrastructure (One Stop Centres, women's helplines, CCTV networks) actually created and made operational using this fund, State-wise;
(c) the amount of the fund that remains unutilised or lying idle as on date; and
(d) the status of compliance with the Supreme Court's directions in Nipun Saxena v. Union of India and Others regarding victim compensation schemes funded from this corpus?

(a) the quantum of loans written off (technically or otherwise) by Public Sector Banks since 2021-22, separately for accounts above ?100 crore, year-wise and bank-wise;
(b) the total number of wilful defaulters declared during this period, company-wise, along with the outstanding amount against each;
(c) out of the written-off amount, how much has actually been recovered, year-wise and what is the recovery rate as a percentage of the total loan written off; and
(d) whether any of the top 50 wilful defaulters by value have since availed fresh credit facilities from any PSU bank or NBFC, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the month-wise international crude oil price versus the retail price of petrol and diesel charged by Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs)in India since 2020;
(b) the month-wise marketing margin earned per litre by OMCs on petrol and diesel during periods when international crude prices fell but retail prices were not reduced;
(c) the total additional revenue earned by OMCs during periods of price stickiness, year-wise; and
(d) whether Petroleum Planning and Analysis Cell has assessed this margin against the reasonable return benchmark used to justify retail price revisions and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the State-wise and crop-wise targets and achievements under various crop diversification programmes since 2021;
(b) the State-wise and crop-wise area brought under crop diversification in water-stressed and groundwater-depleted regions over the last five years;
(c) whether a contingency strategy has been formulated for the forecast of below-normal rainfall and possible monsoon deficiency during the current Kharif season, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the advisories issued to States and farmers regarding crop planning, alternative crops, drought-resilient varieties, sowing schedules and water management for the current season?

(a) the total area under cotton cultivation, productivity and average yield during the last five years upto 2025-26, State-wise, particularly in major cotton-producing States;
(b) the average cost of cultivation, average market price realised by farmers, Minimum Support Price (MSP), procurement and estimated returns from cotton cultivation, State-wise, year-wise;
(c) the decline in cotton acreage in certain States and increasing incidence of pest attacks, particularly pink bollworm and whitefly; and
(d) the details of financial assistance, crop insurance claims and other support provided to farmers affected by pest attacks and crop losses during the last five years, State-wise?

(a) the country-wise details of Memoranda of Understanding and institutional arrangements signed by the Central and State Governments with foreign entities for overseas employment since 2021;
(b) the country-wise, State-wise, and sector-wise details of Indian workers who secured overseas employment through these government-facilitated channels since then;
(c) the country-wise details regarding the nature of employment, skill categories, average wages, contract durations and social security benefits provided under these agreements; and
(d) the institutional mechanisms established to monitor working conditions, verify wages, ensure welfare and handle the grievance redressal of workers employed under these arrangements?

(a) the number of deaths reported during sewer and septic tank cleaning operations in the country during last five years, State-wise, and the number of cases in which compensation, rehabilitation and legal action have been provided;
(b) the reason for continued involvement of manual labour in hazardous sewer and septic tank cleaning despite the prohibition;
(c) the number of inspections, prosecutions recorded against contractors, agencies and officials responsible during the said period; and
(d) whether Government has ensured availability and mandatory use of safety gear, protective measures and training for sanitation workers across municipalities?

(a) the sanctioned intake, actual enrolment and vacant seats in Government and private ITIs during the last five years, State-wise and trade-wise;
(b) whether reasons for persistent ITI vacancies have been assessed, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the trade-wise percentage of ITI graduates employed, pursuing further training, or self-employed over this period;
(d) whether ITI courses are being aligned with current opportunities in IT, healthcare, logistics and emerging technologies; and
(e) whether any independent assessment of ITI reforms, industry linkages and curriculum updates has been conducted?

(a) the fertilizer-wise estimated demand, domestic production, imports, opening stock and total availability of DAP and urea during the current Kharif season;
(b) the State-wise quantity of DAP and urea allocated and supplied against the demand projected by the States during this season;
(c) whether Government has noted any reported shortages of DAP and urea during the ongoing sowing season, including affected States and reasons therefor; and
(d) the source country-wise and timeline-wise quantity of DAP and urea imported during the current financial year?

(a) the feedstock-wise and year-wise quantity of ethanol produced since 2020, specifically from sugarcane juice, B/C-heavy molasses, maize, rice and other feedstocks;
(b) the company-wise and year-wise quantity of ethanol procured by Public Sector Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs) and private entities during this period;
(c) the year-wise procurement price fixed by Government per feedstock category, alongside the estimated production cost and actual price paid by OMCs; and
(d) the total expenditure incurred by OMCs on ethanol procurement during the said period, company-wise and year-wise?

(a) the total number of beneficiaries sanctioned loans under the Prime Minister's Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) since inception, along with the total loan amount sanctioned and margin money subsidy released, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the number of beneficiaries whose margin money subsidy is pending for release, the amount involved and the period for which such subsidy has remained pending, State-wise and district-wise in the State of Haryana; and
(c) the reasons for delay in release of subsidy, indicating the number of cases delayed due to non-availability of funds, procedural delays, bank-related issues or administrative reasons?

(a) the exact number of Indian youth deported from the United States, Mexico and European nations between 2023 and 31st March, 2026, State-wise;
(b) the number of organized human-trafficking and illicit travel-agent syndicates that have been successfully prosecuted and in how many cases punishment was awarded; and
(c) the steps taken by Government for providing compensation and rehabilitation of such deported youth?

(a) the sanctioned strength, working strength and vacancies of teachers in Government schools at the primary, upper primary, secondary and senior secondary levels, State-wise;
(b) the number of Government schools functioning with only one teacher, State-wise and level-wise;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of teacher shortages on learning outcomes and pupil-teacher ratios, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to fill vacant teaching posts and eliminate single-teacher schools?

(a) the value of imports of Active Pharmaceutical Ingredients (APIs), bulk drugs and drug intermediates imported from China during the last three years upto 2025-26, category-wise and year-wise;
(b) the details of major categories of APIs in which India continues to depend on imports from China, indicating domestic production, imports and percentage dependence, category-wise; and
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the strategic risks posed by continued dependence on China for critical APIs and bulk drugs, if so, the details and findings thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the increase in cost of home-cooked vegetarian and non-vegetarian meals during the last one year, due to the rise in prices of essential commodities, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding the impact of rising food prices and below-normal rainfall on household expenditure, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the likely impact of the monsoon and food inflation on the prices of essential commodities, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the annual demand, indigenous production, imports, opening stock, availability and closing stock of Urea, DAP, MOP, NPK, SSP and other major fertilizers during the last five years upto 2025-26, fertilizer-wise and category-wise;
(b) the total quantity of each fertilizer allocated by the Union Government to States against the demanded quantity during the said period, State-wise, fertilizer-wise, category-wise and year-wise; and
(c) the total amount allocated and released by Government towards fertilizer subsidy during the last five years upto 2025-26, fertilizer-wise, category-wise and year-wise?

(a) the category-wise number of E10/E20-compatible vehicles versus pure-petrol vehicles currently operational in the country;
(b) whether older, pre-E20 vehicles face operational issues such as mileage drop, fuel pump corrosion or engine clogging due to ethanol blends;
(c) whether running E20 blended petrol requires flex-engine technology that is largely absent in the existing vehicle fleet; and
(d) if so, whether Government has arranged for the parallel supply of unblended regular petrol for non-E20 compatible vehicles?

(a) the number of airports developed under UDAN scheme till date and number of airports that are currently operational, including cost of development of each airport separately;
(b) the number of commercial flights undertaken from each airport since 2021 uptil 31st March, 2026; and
(c) the number of Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS) aerodromes that have achieved financial self-sustainability after the three-year Operation and Maintenance (O&M) support window?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of the significant decline in India’s household savings rate in recent years, with financial indicators showing a marked reduction in savings as a share of GDP;
(b) the year-wise data on household savings and liabilities for the last five years, including financial and non-financial savings and credit uptake; and
(c) the assessment of the macroeconomic and socio-economic implications of this trend for long-term investment, financial resilience of households and future growth, along with the corrective measures being taken to strengthen savings and reduce over-dependence on credit?

(a) the number of active beneficiaries under Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) between 2020–21 to 2025–26, year-wise, State-wise;
(b) the number of beneficiaries rendered inactive or excluded during the same period due to e-KYC, Aadhaar seeding or land record verification issues, year-wise, with reasons therefor; and
(c) whether there is a proposal to increase the amount given to beneficiaries, in view of the massive increase in input costs, particularly the prices of diesel, fertilizers and land rent, etc.?

(a) the current status of the Bharatmala Pariyojana, including the total length of highway projects approved, awarded and completed between 2021-22 to 2024-25;
(b) the reasons for delays in the implementation of certain projects under the scheme and the measures taken to address these delays;
(c) whether Government has decided to halt the initiation of new projects under the Bharatmala Pariyojana and if so, the rationale behind this decision;
(d) the revised timeline and estimated cost for the completion of the remaining projects under the scheme; and
(e) the steps being taken to ensure timely completion of the ongoing projects and to mitigate cost overruns?

(a) whether Government takes cognizance that India accounts for nearly 25 per cent of the global tuberculosis burden despite a 21 per cent decline between 2015–2024 and the reasons for not meeting the 2025 national TB elimination target;
(b) the measures taken to address India’s high TB share in 2024 -2025 and whether drug shortages, treatment discontinuation or diagnostic delays have been recorded or audited; and
(c) the State-wise availability and stock-out record of essential MDR-TB drugs and rapid molecular diagnostic kits since 2022 and whether rural and aspirational districts face diagnostic or treatment delays?

(a) whether Government has observed an increase in cancer incidence and mortality rates across various regions in the country over the past five years;
(b) if so, the details of cancer incidence, mortality and survival rates from 2019-20 to 2024-25, State-wise, gender-wise and cancer type-wise;
(c) whether environmental factors such as industrial pollution, pesticide exposure and contaminated water sources have been identified as contributing to the rise in cancer cases, particularly in rural and industrial areas; and
(d) the current status of oncology infrastructure in high-burden regions, including the number of cancer care facilities, availability of specialized medical personnel and accessibility of treatment services?

(a) whether Government notes that India is likely to miss the USD 1 trillion export target for financial year 2026, despite signing multiple Free Trade Agreements (FTAs);
(b) the reasons as to why FTAs have not translated into anticipated export gains, particularly in key markets;
(c) the assessment of export performance, sector-wise and destination-wise, including the impact of tariffs and non-tariff barriers; and
(d) the strategic adjustments or corrective measures Government proposes to ensure that India remains competitive globally and achieves its export aspirations?

(a) the sanctioned strength, present filled strength and the number of vacancies for each CAPF;
(b) what is the position of actual funds released vs required/demanded funds for CAPF modernisation projects in the last five years; and
(c) the timeline to clear the identified manpower and capital shortfalls and whether a contingency fund has been created to meet urgent CAPF operational needs?

(a) whether Government has conducted an independent inquiry into the allegations of contamination in cough syrups produced by Indian pharmaceutical companies, if so, the findings thereof and the actions taken;
(b) the number of licenses revoked or suspended for manufacturing the affected cough syrup brands;
(c) the compensation, if any, provided to the families of the victims; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure accountability in the pharmaceutical industry to prevent such incidents?

(a) the year-wise total outstanding debt of the Union Government for the last five years i.e., 2020-21 to 2024-25;
(b) the details of internal and external debt components, year-wise during the same period;
(c) the ratio of the total Union Government debt to GDP in each of these years; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to reduce the overall debt burden?
BPN

(a) the number of PM MITRA Parks planned, initiated and fully operational as on date, details thereof, State-wise;
(b) the land area allotted, investment committed, jobs created and export value generated by each operational PM MITRA Park;
(c) the year-wise progress against original timelines and reasons for any delays or stalls since inception; and
(d) the assessment of impact on India’s textile competitiveness and export performance vis-à-vis major competing countries?

(a) the list of Central and State digital portals used for procurement of crops at Minimum Support Price (MSP) and also the number of farmers denied MSP procurement due to digital/registration failures in the last 24 months, State-wise;
(b) the State-wise total estimated production and procurement of cotton by Cotton Corporation of India (CCI) during Kharif 2025-26 and also the number of farmers denied MSP owing to the glitches/failures in the CCI app; and
(c) measures taken to compensate farmers denied MSP either on account of App failure or otherwise including payment of difference by Government and the amounts released, particularly for Cotton, Bajara, Moong and other Kharif crops?

(a) the number of Indian nationals, deported from the United States and other countries during the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the number of travel agents or middlemen investigated, arrested or prosecuted for organising such migration routes and the amount recovered from them;
(c) whether Government has formally protested with the United States and other countries regarding inhumane treatment of deported Indian citizens;
(d) the preventive measures, including registration or licensing of travel agencies and border coordination taken to protect vulnerable youth; and
(e) whether any targets or timelines have been fixed to reduce illegal “Dunki route” migration and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the year-wise analysis of accuracy of cyclone forecasts issued by the India Meteorological Department (IMD) during the last five years, including lead time and track/intensity prediction accuracy;
(b) the number of cyclones making landfall in India each year during that period and the number of lives lost in each of these events, district-wise; and
(c) the steps taken to strengthen real-time forecasting, impact-based warnings, community dissemination systems and infrastructure resilience in cyclone-prone regions?

(a) the total number of missing persons, specifically women, girls and minors, State-wise, in the country from 2020–21 to 2024–25, along with the number of cases registered;
(b) the number of human trafficking gangs operating State-wise across the country, including action taken, FIRs lodged and convictions secured against organised human trafficking networks; and
(c) the relief and rehabilitation measures, including grant of compensation to victims of human trafficking and details of year-wise compensation paid during the last five years?

(a) whether Government has detected harmful manufacture/sale of over the counter (OTC) Medicines/liquid syrups being sold in the coutnry, if so, the details of such medicines and syrups;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the existing standards and protocols for the manufacturing/sale of over-the-counter (OTC) medicines including liquid syrups in light of the recent incidents involving contaminated cough syrups; and
(c) if so, the specific changes made, protocols enforced or enhancements made to the regulatory framework?

(a) the total Government collection from Surcharges and Cesses, year-wise and specific Surcharge/ Cess wise for the years 2020 -21 to 2024 -25, including utilisation thereof and the details of unspent funds, year-wise and head-wise;
(b) the reasons as to why a substantial portion of these funds have not been allocated for the intended purposes such as health, education and infrastructure; and
(c) whether Government plans to share the funds collected from Surcharges/Cesses with the States, if so, the methodology thereof?

(a) total funds allocated and the actual expenditure incurred under the Production-Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for drone manufacturers during the last three Financial Years;
(b) whether it is a fact that 90 per cent of equipment being used for manufacture of drones by the manufactures is of chinese origin;
(c) the reasons for underutilization of approximately 18 per cent of total outlay of ?120 crores under the PLI scheme;
(d) the percentage of drone flight controllers sourced from Chinese manufacturers during the last five years; and
(e) plan of Government to enhance transparency and accountability in the management and allocation of funds for the same?

(a) the number of gig/platform workers registered on e-Shram as on 31 Mar 2025 and the number actually onboarded onto specific social security entitlements since Budget 2025 commitments;
(b) evaluation of pilot aggregator onboarding and what percentage of registered workers received active benefits and what technical/legal barriers remain to aggregator compliance;
(c) whether the Ministry has a roadmap to extend PMJAY/DBT benefits to one crore gig workers as announced in Budget 2025 and the interim safeguards to prevent exclusion; and
(d) steps to ensure interoperability between e-Shram, PMJAY and State welfare registries so benefits reach gig workers irrespective of platform affiliation?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance that scrapping the 11 per cent import duty on cotton has reduced domestic prices, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has provided assistance to cotton farmers affected by low prices, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether cotton imports from the United States of America (USA) have increased after the duty was removed and the details thereof; and
(d) the quantity of cotton purchased by the Cotton Corporation of India (CCI) at MSP over the last five years, including Kharif 2025–26, compared with total production in the respective years?

(a) the number of Indian nationals identified as illegally working/forced to work in the Russian Army along with the count of fatalities/missing since 2022 till date;
(b) the Indian nationals currently estimated to be stuck working in the Russian Army as on date and the dates of all communications exchanged between the Ministry and Russia seeking their repatriation;
(c) whether the mortal remains of any Indians killed in the Russia-Ukraine war are yet to be repatriated and if so, the reasons for the delay; and
(d) the steps being taken to ensure the immediate repatriation of remaining Indians?

(a) the year-wise enrolment in Government schools during the last three years;
(b) the total vacancy of teachers in Government schools during the last three years;
(c) the number of Government schools without sufficient classrooms, toilets, electricity and other basic infrastructure as per the norms fixed; and
(d) whether non-availability of teachers, insufficient classrooms, non - availability of toilets (including toilets for girl students), lack of electricity and basic infrastructure are the principal reasons for decline in enrolments?

(a) the budget allocation and actual expenditure for Mission Saksham Anganwadi & POSHAN 2.0 from FY 2020 to 2025;
(b) State-wise details for number of Anganwadi Centres upgraded vs. approved targets and the count of vacant Anganwadi Workers/AWW posts all over the country, particularly in priority/aspirational districts; and
(c) the monitoring metrics and evaluated impact on child malnutrition indicators (stunting/wasting) over the last five years?

(a) the expected GST revenue shortfall due to GST rationalisation, whether Government will provide additional compensation to States facing losses;
(b) whether Government will share Cesses or Surcharges with States to offset revenue loss from GST rationalisation;
(c) whether Government has examined ITC issues where higher-taxed raw materials and lower-taxed finished goods raise consumer prices; and
(d) whether there is any plan to reduce GST on pencils, stationery and other essential items for children and education?

(a) the total number of airports handed over to private players for operation, management or development, with names of companies, concession periods and airport details;
(b) details of airports privatised since 2020, year-wise;
(c) whether any reports exist of increased passenger service fees, airport charges or disputes after privatisation, and the steps taken to address them; and
(d) whether Government plans to privatise more airports in the near future, and the details thereof?
bs

(a) the details of the wholesale mandi prices of major kharif crops as on 24 October 2025, juxtaposed with their respective Minimum Support Prices (MSPs);
(b) the number/proportion of farmers who were able to sell at or above MSP, minus any deductions, during the kharif 2025-26 harvest so far, crop-wise and State-wise;
(c) the crop-wise procurement of Kharif crops in 2025 -26 at MSP by Government; and
(d) the State-wise compensation released by Government for damage of Kharif crop owing to floods and incessant rains?

(a) a consolidated upto date assessment of Production Linked Incentive Scheme (PLI) scheme results and whether the PLI has demonstrably improved Micro Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) integration into global value chains;
(b) the causes identified for the recent temporary slowdown/volatility in merchandise exports and the steps taken to stabilise MSME exporters;
(c) whether any sectoral impact evaluation of PLI on export competitiveness has been completed, if so, its key findings; and
(d) the package of immediate measures proposed to shield MSME exporters from external shocks (tariff barriers, logistics costs, input inflation) while ensuring PLI benefits reach subcontracting MSMEs?

(a) the number of doping cases reported in the country during the last five years, sport-wise and year-wise including the number of doping violations involving minor athletes (under the age of 18) during the same period;
(b) whether Government proposes to strengthen the frequency and coverage of anti-doping tests, both in-competition and out-of-competition, particularly at grassroots and junior levels;
(c) the steps taken by Government and NADA to promote awareness, education and prevention of doping among athletes, coaches and support staff; and
(d) whether any rehabilitation or reintegration mechanisms exist for athletes who have completed their doping suspension?

(a) whether nearly 10,000 posts in Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVs) and nearly 8,000 posts in Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas are vacant as of August, 2025;
(b) how much of Kendriya Vidyalaya Sanghatan funds have remained unspent year-wise, along with year-wise budgetary allocation over last five years; and
(c) whether no permanent posts were filled in Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas (JNVs) during 2023-24 & 2024-25 including reasons for large vacancies and funds underutilization?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports regarding the discharge of untreated sewage from residential colonies, slum settlements and cattle pounds along the Pinjore-Mallah Road into the Kaushalya river in Panchkula, the State of Haryana;
(b) whether the Central Government has received any complaints or reports from the State Government or other agencies regarding the contamination of the Kaushalya Dam reservoir; and
(c) whether the Central Government has taken cognizance of violations of National Green Tribunal guidelines in this context and if so, details of any directions or advisories issued to the State Government for compliance with these norms?

(a) whether Government is aware of reports regarding widespread illegal and unregulated sand mining along the banks and bed of the Yamuna river, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the impact of illegal sand mining on the Yamuna Action Plan (YAP), particularly with respect to pollution control, flow regulation and river rejuvenation; and
(c) the details of action taken including the number of FIRs lodged, persons arrested, and convictions made in connection with violations under the YAP?

(a) the total number of students enrolled or placed under Prime Minister’s Internship Scheme (PMIS) in the last three years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) whether the uptake of the scheme has remained below expectations, if so, the reasons identified for the same including relocation issues, stipend adequacy and mismatch in job roles;
(c) the total target for internship placements under PMIS in financial year 2025–26 and the roadmap to achieve the 10 million internship target in the next five years; and
(d) the total budgetary allocation and expenditure under the scheme since inception, including the provision for financial year 2025–26?

(a) the number of COVID-19 deaths reported separately by the Civil Registration System (CRS), Medical Certification of Cause of Death (MCCD), and the Ministry's official dashboard for 2020 and 2021;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any reconciliatory exercise to standardise and publish a single, authoritative national death toll from COVID-19; and
(c) whether Government proposes to revise the official COVID-19 death figures in light of significantly higher all-cause mortality reflected in CRS and MCCD data during the same period, and the details thereof?

(a) the total amount of loans written off by public sector and scheduled private sector banks during each of the last five years, including Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) the amount recovered from these written-off loans by these banks during the same period;
(c) whether the sharp rise in write-offs by private sector banks in Financial Year 2025-26 indicates any dilution in underwriting standards and worsening of asset quality, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures being undertaken to ensure better recovery rates from written-off accounts and to strengthen the overall financial health of the banking sector?

(a) the criteria and rationale for declaring any city a smart city;
(b) the total number of smart city projects announced, operational, completed, State-wise along with the total funds allocated and utilised, year-wise;
(c) the total number of smart cities which has crossed the normal threshold in air pollution and considered polluted across the country, State-wise; and
(d) whether there is any provision of including the pollution and urban flood mitigation strategies in designated smart cities, if so, the details thereof?
SS

(a) the total complaints or cases related to sale and circulation of adulterated and substandard fertilisers and seeds during the last three years, State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has conducted inspections, raids or surveillance operations to identify and take action against such illegal practices; and
(c) whether there are any loopholes in the regulatory oversight or vigilance in curbing such activity, if so, the details thereof and the steps taken to prevent the production and sale of adulterated agri inputs?

(a) whether Government is aware of large-scale felling of indigenous tree species, including the protected Khejri tree, for solar projects in arid and semi-arid zones of Rajasthan;
(b) whether any reports have been received from Rajasthan or other agencies regarding violations of environmental norms or lack of clearances;
(c) whether Government plans to strengthen guidelines to regulate tree felling and enforce stricter safeguards for solar and infrastructure projects on non-forest land; and
(d) whether stronger legal protection and revised afforestation policies are being considered for ecologically sensitive arid regions?

(a) whether Government has approved the procurement of a Polar Research Vessel (PRV) to support India's polar expeditions and research activities;
(b) if so, the timeline and estimated cost initially approved for the project;
(c) the current status of the PRV procurement and the reasons for the prolonged delay in its acquisition;
(d) whether the delay has affected India’s research capabilities in the Antarctic and Arctic regions; and
(e) the revised timeline, if any, for commissioning the vessel and the measures being taken to expedite the process?

(a) the number of calls received and resolved through the National helpline for prevention of atrocities against SCs/STs, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) the categorised data on the nature of atrocities reported through the helpline and the number of such cases resolved; and
(c) the criteria or official metric used by Government to classify a complaint as an atrocity under the relevant legal framework?

(a) the number of loans sanctioned under the newly introduced ‘Tarun Plus’ category of MUDRA loan scheme; 
(b) whether there is any mechanism to track the long-term growth or scale-up of enterprises that move from Tarun to Tarun Plus, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether there is any additional incentive or support systems being provided to successful repeat borrowers under the scheme, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of fake firms detected under the GST regime during the last five years;
(b) the total amount of fraudulent Input Tax Credit (ITC) claimed by such fake firms during these two years;
(c) the amount of ITC recovered during this period and the number of arrests made in connection with ITC frauds;
(d) the revenue loss due to such fraudulent ITC claims on the overall GST revenue collection;
(e) the steps taken by Government to prevent fraudulent GST registrations and ITC claims; and
(f) the system in place to track repeated offenders or mastermind networks behind these fake firms?
G

(a) whether Government now proposes to revise the ethanol blending target to 30 per cent by 2030, if so, the timeline and roadmap for achieving the revised target;
(b) the total quantity of ethanol blended with petrol during the last five years and the breakup of ethanol procured from sugar-based and grain-based sources; and
(c) the steps taken by Government to ensure a steady supply of ethanol considering growing demand and its impact on sugar production/availability?

(a) the total value of trade conducted through electronic National Agriculture Market (e-NAM) during the last five years;
(b) whether the volume of inter-State trade on e-NAM platform has declined in Financial Year 2025, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the total number of mandis, traders, Farmer Producer Organisations (FPOs), commission agents and farmers currently registered on e-NAM platform;
(d) whether Government acknowledges that inter-State and inter-mandi trade remain minimal despite onboarding of over 1,400 mandis, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps to address the logistical gaps that are hindering inter-State trade, including partnerships with logistics and value-added service providers?

(a) whether Government is aware of the emergence of a radical group backed by Turkey in Bangladesh involved in promoting a ‘Greater Bangladesh’ map that includes parts of Indian territory, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has raised the issue diplomatically with the Government of Bangladesh and/or Turkey, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has assessed the security implications of increased Turkish and Pakistani engagement in Bangladesh, if so, the steps taken in this regard; and
(d) the measures being taken to counter radical propaganda, secure India’s northeastern region, and enhance border surveillance with Bangladesh?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the adequacy of the existing national poverty line in light of evolving consumption patterns and cost of living;
(b) whether the poverty line has been revised over the last five years despite inflation and changes in consumption patterns;
(c) whether Government proposes to update the national poverty line more frequently, in order to reflect current cost of living conditions in rural and urban areas; and
(d) whether any steps have been taken to introduce dynamic poverty estimation mechanisms using interim indicators such as inflation and expenditure growth, in the absence of frequent consumption surveys?

(a) whether it is a fact that despite a decade since the launch of the 'Make in India' initiative, the manufacturing sector’s share in the GDP has shown no significant improvement;
(b) if so, the reasons for the same despite various policy measures and incentive schemes;
(c) whether Government considers the initiative successful in generating employment and enhancing domestic industrial capacity;
(d) the steps being taken to address key bottlenecks such as slow technology adoption and challenges in Ease of Doing Business; and
(e) whether Government proposes any course correction or audit of the initiative?

(a) whether Government has discontinued the National Fellowship Scheme for Scheduled Tribes, Scheduled Castes and other economically and socially disadvantaged students pursuing M.Phil and Ph.D since 2023;
